  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Song of Solomon",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 2,
    "summary": "Beloved ones are praised and described.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "I am the rose of Sharon, and the lily of the valleys.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 2,
            "end": 4
          },
          {
            "start": 25,
            "end": 28
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 2:1",
        "book": "Song of Solomon",
        "chapter": 2,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "As the lily among thorns, so is my love among the daughters.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 29,
            "end": 31
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 2:2",
        "book": "Song of Solomon",
        "chapter": 2,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "As the apple tree among the trees of the wood, so is my beloved among the sons. I sat down under his shadow with great delight, and his fruit was sweet to my taste.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 50,
            "end": 52
          },
          {
            "start": 142,
            "end": 145
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 2:3",
        "book": "Song of Solomon",
        "chapter": 2,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "He brought me to the banqueting house, and his banner over me was love.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 62,
            "end": 65
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 2:4",
        "book": "Song of Solomon",
        "chapter": 2,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "Stay me with flagons, comfort me with apples: for I am sick of love.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 22,
            "end": 32,
            "text": "IE refresh me."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 52,
            "end": 54
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 2:5",
        "book": "Song of Solomon",
        "chapter": 2,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "His left hand is under my head, and his right hand doth embrace me.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 14,
            "end": 16
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 2:6",
        "book": "Song of Solomon",
        "chapter": 2,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "I charge you, O ye daughters of Jerusalem, by the roes, and by the hinds of the field, that ye stir not up, nor awake my love, till he please.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 118,
            "end": 120
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 2:7",
        "book": "Song of Solomon",
        "chapter": 2,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "The voice of my beloved! behold, he cometh leaping upon the mountains, skipping upon the hills.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 2:8",
        "book": "Song of Solomon",
        "chapter": 2,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "My beloved is like a roe or a young hart: behold, he standeth behind our wall, he looketh forth at the windows, shewing himself through the lattice.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 36,
            "end": 40,
            "text": "OR gazelle, fawn."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 2:9",
        "book": "Song of Solomon",
        "chapter": 2,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "My beloved spake, and said unto me, Rise up, my love, my fair one, and come away.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 2:10",
        "book": "Song of Solomon",
        "chapter": 2,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "For, lo, the winter is past, the rain is over and gone;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 46,
            "end": 49
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 2:11",
        "book": "Song of Solomon",
        "chapter": 2,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "The flowers appear on the earth; the time of the singing of birds is come, and the voice of the turtle is heard in our land;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 11,
            "text": "TG Nature, Earth."
          },
          {
            "start": 96,
            "end": 102,
            "text": "IE turtle-dove. Jer. 8:7."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 57,
            "end": 65
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Nature, Earth.",
            "prettyString": "TG Nature, Earth",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Nature, Earth",
                "entryId": "tg-nature-earth",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 2:12",
        "book": "Song of Solomon",
        "chapter": 2,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "The fig tree putteth forth her green figs, and the vines with the tender grape give a good smell. Arise, my love, my fair one, and come away.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 57,
            "end": 61
          },
          {
            "start": 86,
            "end": 90
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 2:13",
        "book": "Song of Solomon",
        "chapter": 2,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "O my dove, that art in the clefts of the rock, in the secret places of the stairs, let me see thy countenance, let me hear thy voice; for sweet is thy voice, and thy countenance is comely.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 19
          },
          {
            "start": 61,
            "end": 67
          },
          {
            "start": 144,
            "end": 146
          },
          {
            "start": 178,
            "end": 180
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 2:14",
        "book": "Song of Solomon",
        "chapter": 2,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "Take us the foxes, the little foxes, that spoil the vines: for our vines have tender grapes.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 73,
            "end": 77
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 2:15",
        "book": "Song of Solomon",
        "chapter": 2,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "My beloved is mine, and I am his: he feedeth among the lilies.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 13
          },
          {
            "start": 26,
            "end": 28
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 2:16",
        "book": "Song of Solomon",
        "chapter": 2,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "Until the day break, and the shadows flee away, turn, my beloved, and be thou like a roe or a young hart upon the mountains of Bether.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 17,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 2:17",
        "book": "Song of Solomon",
        "chapter": 2,
        "verse": 17
      }
    ]
  },
